Well, lawful players when Crowned become the Hand of Elbereth, chaotic
players become the Glory of Arioch... so how about Arioch's name as an
inscription? Causes conflict in all non-@ monsters that see the player
(or are within a certain distance of him), so they are more likely to
attack each other (but can still attack the player). A monster summoning
other monsters might be an actual benefit as it would tend to attack
them (if under conflict) as likely as attack you.

(Orcus summons Demogorgon! Demogorgon hits Orcus! -more-)

Neutrals, of course, get called the "Envoy of Balance", but perhaps they
need a better title with some kind of name or other. Then inscribing
that name could be made to mean something.

Oh, and then... You should only be able to use ONE of the inscriptions,
and that one based on your alignment. Non-lawfuls shouldn't be able to
use Elbereth, non-chaotics shouldn't be able to call on Arioch's name,
non-neutrals shouldn't be able to inscribe the name of whatever the
Neutral crowning-glory's name is changed to. Of course, this would mean
that there is a benefit to being lawful (as Elbereth is a damn good
inscription), which would counter the penalty of being thrown back
further and more often when coming back up with the Amulet - chaotics
and neutrals don't get thrown back as far or as often, but they wouldn't
have the benefit either. Your choice...

Better still, make this only happen when you've been crowned - if you
haven't been crowned, no inscribing works at all. (At the moment,
crowning is as much a hindrance as a help - you can get all the
intrinsics from elsewhere anyway, and the main effect is to wreck your
prayer timeout, whereas it should be more boon than bane.)

And if you change your base alignment while crowned, you should lose ALL
the benefits of crowning (even if you got them independently: since
crowning provides fire and cold resistance, you should lose these, even
if you got them from some other means than being crowned) and be no
longer crowned. You can, of course, collect up the beneficial intrinsics
again in whatever way you want, and possibly be crowned a second time by
your new god...

